The action contributes to mainstreaming climate change adaptation processes in the agriculture and food system through enhancing resilient seed systems and promoting quality seeds of climate tolerant varieties. 
In 2023, FAO will conduct the following activities:
•	National professionals training on seed propagation, breeding technologies and variety recovery;
•	Finalization of the national seed system assessment report;
•	Finalization of the National Seed portfolio and publishing it online for wider audience;
•	National workshop for presentation of the project results;
•	Publication of the national legal situation on seed production.

